{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9000000000000030","type":"group","x":0,"y":2002,"width":3200,"height":1696,"label":"③ The program — six clusters, twenty directions → CoWAM"},
		{"id":"9000000000000020","type":"group","x":0,"y":1068,"width":3200,"height":898,"label":"② The gap — six clusters, one gap apiece"},
		{"id":"9000000000000050","type":"group","x":0,"y":4314,"width":3200,"height":794,"label":"⑤ What to build — gate-driven, not a timeline"},
		{"id":"9000000000000010","type":"group","x":0,"y":476,"width":3200,"height":556,"label":"① Physics & first principles — why the coupling term exists"},
		{"id":"9000000000000040","type":"group","x":0,"y":3734,"width":3200,"height":544,"label":"④ First experiments — one cluster falsifier per coupling cluster"},
		{"id":"9000000000000060","type":"group","x":0,"y":5144,"width":3200,"height":504,"label":"⑥ Benchmarks — humanoid suites only"},
		{"id":"9000000000000000","type":"group","x":0,"y":0,"width":3200,"height":440,"label":"Focus-Direction Workflow · CoWAM program pitch"},
		{"id":"9000000000000070","type":"group","x":0,"y":5684,"width":3200,"height":448,"label":"⑦ Risks & fallbacks — every branch yields a result"},
		{"id":"9000000000000080","type":"group","x":0,"y":6144,"width":3200,"height":384,"label":"What I am asking"},
		{"id":"9300000000000001","type":"group","x":40,"y":2778,"width":480,"height":900,"color":"4","label":"WB.A · arm↔leg (green core)"},
		{"id":"9300000000000002","type":"group","x":560,"y":2778,"width":480,"height":732,"color":"4","label":"WB.B · base↔arm (green core)"},
		{"id":"9300000000000003","type":"group","x":1080,"y":2778,"width":480,"height":564,"color":"4","label":"WB.C · force-under-load (green core)"},
		{"id":"9300000000000004","type":"group","x":1640,"y":2778,"width":480,"height":732,"color":"5","label":"WAM.A · predict (cyan)"},
		{"id":"9300000000000005","type":"group","x":2160,"y":2778,"width":480,"height":900,"color":"5","label":"Sim2Real.B · ground (cyan)"},
		{"id":"9300000000000006","type":"group","x":2680,"y":2778,"width":480,"height":900,"color":"5","label":"Embodied-AI.B · verify (cyan)"},
		{"id":"a000000000000001","type":"text","text":"# CoWAM · Coupling-aware World-Action Model\n## Focus-Direction Workflow — the program pitch\n*One bet: make the whole-body couplings a humanoid policy normally discards **explicit and anticipatory**. Read top → bottom: seven rows, then the ask. Every node is colored by the legend on the right.*","x":20,"y":20,"width":2000,"height":170},
		{"id":"a000000000000002","type":"text","text":"> [!abstract] The bet\n> Attack whole-body humanoid capability across **six clusters at once**: three **coupling** clusters as the co-equal core (the **green** spine) and three **mechanism** clusters that supply and complement it (the **cyan** layer).\n>\n> **Green core → CoWAM:** make the discarded couplings explicit + anticipatory — **WB.A arm↔leg** (self-induced inertial), **WB.B base↔arm** (kinematic), **WB.C force-under-load** (external wrench).\n>\n> **Cyan mechanisms** (each a standalone embodied-AI advance that also wires CoWAM's loop): **WAM.A predict**, **Sim2Real.B ground**, **Embodied-AI.B verify**.\n>\n> The bet: a cheap, structured physics term — predicted, grounded, verified — beats far larger data + compute on a fixed budget, and can prove itself wrong up front.","x":20,"y":210,"width":2000,"height":210},
		{"id":"a000000000000003","type":"text","text":"> [!note] Color legend & how to read\n> 🟩 **green** — coupling core (CoWAM): WB.A / WB.B / WB.C, the bet\n> 🟦 **cyan** — mechanism clusters: WAM.A predict · Sim2Real.B ground · Embodied-AI.B verify (also standalone advances)\n> 🟥 **red** — reactive foils, what fails today\n> 🟧 **orange** — headline benchmark axes\n> 🟪 **purple** — deferred extension (C2 certified safe set)\n> ⬜ **grey** — context that recedes (deploy surface, substrate)\n>\n> **Rows, top → bottom:** ① Physics · ② Gap · ③ Program (6 clusters) · ④ Falsifiers · ⑤ What to build · ⑥ Benchmarks · ⑦ Risks → **the Ask**.","x":2060,"y":20,"width":1120,"height":400},
		{"id":"a100000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: whole-body control is conventionally split into an arm controller and a balance controller, with the coupling left implicit. The physics says that split throws away real terms — make them explicit and anticipatory.*","x":20,"y":512,"width":3160,"height":64},
		{"id":"a100000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Arm reach**\ncommanded q̈_arm","x":40,"y":604,"width":240,"height":96},
		{"id":"a100000000000002","type":"text","text":"**× M(base,arm)**\noff-diagonal block of M(q)","x":320,"y":604,"width":280,"height":96},
		{"id":"a100000000000003","type":"text","text":"**Base / leg reaction**\nδ_base = M(base,arm)·q̈_arm","x":648,"y":604,"width":300,"height":96},
		{"id":"a100000000000004","type":"text","text":"Part-wise control **discards** δ_base → instability on fast reaches","x":1000,"y":576,"width":330,"height":92,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a100000000000005","type":"text","text":"**CoWAM** predicts δ_base **before** it hits (explicit + anticipatory)","x":1000,"y":700,"width":330,"height":92,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a100000000000006","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] First principles · the program bet\n> **First principle:** M(q) is non-block-diagonal → every whole-body motion transmits a low-dimensional, structured cross-term (a reaction wrench, or a kinematic feasibility constraint) between arm, base, legs — a quantity to **predict**, not data to collect.\n> **Assumption challenged:** the field decouples whole-body control into an arm controller + a balance controller and leaves the coupling implicit or reactive.\n> **The bet:** making each coupling explicit, anticipatory, grounded, verified beats far larger data + compute on a fixed budget — gain concentrated where the cross-term is largest — and it falsifies cheaply via the ε-curve.","x":40,"y":812,"width":1290,"height":200},
		{"id":"a100000000000007","type":"text","text":"**The coupling physics — three channels part-wise control discards** (green core)","x":1380,"y":576,"width":840,"height":56},
		{"id":"a100000000000008","type":"text","text":"**WB.A · arm↔leg** — self-induced inertial\nδ_base = M(base,arm)·q̈_arm","x":1380,"y":644,"width":840,"height":92,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a100000000000009","type":"text","text":"**WB.C · force-under-load** — external wrench\nδ_ext = J_ext^T·F_ext   *(A + C share one output head)*","x":1380,"y":748,"width":840,"height":92,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a10000000000000a","type":"text","text":"**WB.B · base↔arm** — kinematic\nthe base is itself a manipulation DoF *(separate kinematic head)*","x":1380,"y":852,"width":840,"height":92,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a10000000000000b","type":"text","text":"**The three enablers — each also a standalone breakthrough** (cyan)","x":2260,"y":576,"width":900,"height":56},
		{"id":"a10000000000000c","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A · predict** — architecture + training that carries the cross-term on a world-action latent","x":2260,"y":644,"width":900,"height":92,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a10000000000000d","type":"text","text":"**Sim2Real.B · ground** — differentiable system-ID makes the imagined physics real (robot-self sysID)","x":2260,"y":748,"width":900,"height":92,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a10000000000000e","type":"text","text":"**Embodied-AI.B · verify** — a causal-consistency metric binding predicted → realized coupling","x":2260,"y":852,"width":900,"height":92,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a200000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: each coupling is handled today — but reactively, implicitly, or one-directionally — never anticipatory inside one coupled humanoid policy; and the predict / ground / verify seams are unwired. Six clusters, one gap apiece.*","x":20,"y":1104,"width":3160,"height":56},
		{"id":"a200000000000001","type":"text","text":"**The coupling core (green) leaves all three channels on the table** — each anchor shown with the gap it leaves","x":40,"y":1170,"width":2400,"height":40},
		{"id":"a200000000000002","type":"text","text":"**WB.A · arm↔leg — handled _implicitly_**\n[[2604.07993|HEX]]'s predictive MoE never makes the inertial cross-term an explicit term; [[2606.16542|ADAPT]] reacts after the fact.","x":40,"y":1218,"width":760,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a200000000000003","type":"text","text":"**WB.B · base↔arm — handled _one-directionally_**\n[[2507.01961|AC-DiT]] conditions base→arm only; [[2401.02117|Mobile ALOHA]] flat-concats and lets drift accumulate.","x":840,"y":1218,"width":760,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a200000000000004","type":"text","text":"**WB.C · force-under-load — handled _reactively_**\n[[2505.06776|FALCON]] / [[2510.26280|Thor]] / [[2606.03297|SplitAdapter]] estimate-then-compensate from the past; [[2201.03871|ALMA]] anticipates only the _known_ self-wrench, on a quadruped, in a separate policy.","x":1640,"y":1218,"width":760,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a2f0000000000005","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2505.06776-method.png","x":1640,"y":1350,"width":319,"height":200},
		{"id":"a200000000000005","type":"text","text":"🟥 **reactive foil** — ADAPT estimates the wrench _after_ it manifests","x":430,"y":1556,"width":370,"height":52,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a200000000000006","type":"text","text":"🟥 **reactive foil** — FALCON / Thor / SplitAdapter compensate from the _past_","x":1640,"y":1556,"width":370,"height":52,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a200000000000007","type":"text","text":"**The three enabler seams (cyan) are each unwired**","x":40,"y":1608,"width":2400,"height":40},
		{"id":"a200000000000008","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A · predict** — world-action models imagine _scene_ futures ([[2411.04983|DINO-WM]], [[2504.02792|UWM]], [[2603.14482|V-JEPA 2.1]]); **none output an anticipatory coupling-wrench** as a modeled physics quantity.","x":40,"y":1656,"width":1020,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a200000000000009","type":"text","text":"**Sim2Real.B · ground** — differentiable system-ID recovers _object_ physics ([[2603.01151|D-REX]]); **never re-pointed at the robot's own M(base,arm) + contact model** (the self physics).","x":1090,"y":1656,"width":1020,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a20000000000000a","type":"text","text":"**Embodied-AI.B · verify** — WM-eval harnesses score _fidelity / plausibility_ ([[2606.05773|PiL-World]], [[2606.18610|SC3-Eval]]); **none certify the causal binding** of predicted → realized coupling.","x":2140,"y":1656,"width":1020,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a20000000000000b","type":"text","text":"> [!warning] The honest headline (do not oversell)\n> The well-known **41% → 62%** OOD margin is **borrowed**: it is [[2604.07993|HEX]]-implicit beating part-wise stacks (implicit-vs-part-wise, on arm↔leg) — the **field's** proof-of-life, **not my claim**. My testable wedge per channel is **explicit-vs-implicit** (and on the two force channels A, C, **explicit-vs-reactive**), which each falsifier _tests_, not a number already in hand.","x":40,"y":1796,"width":2050,"height":150},
		{"id":"a20000000000000c","type":"text","text":"**The gap in one line:** no prior work makes the inertial cross-term (A) _or_ the unknown external wrench (C) an **explicit, anticipatory world-model output inside one coupled humanoid policy**, nor binds **predicted → realized coupling** as a metric — and predict / ground / verify each leave the matching seam unwired.","x":2120,"y":1796,"width":1040,"height":150},
		{"id":"a300000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: the program improves each cluster **as a whole** — advancing all its directions together as one artifact, not isolated point fixes. Green = the co-equal coupling core; cyan = the predict / ground / verify mechanism seams (also standalone advances). They compose into one deployable model: **CoWAM**.*","x":20,"y":2038,"width":3160,"height":56},
		{"id":"a300000000000001","type":"text","text":"The coupling head (predict A+C wrench, factor B) **plugs onto any WAM backbone**, grounded (S2R.B) and verified (EAI.B):","x":40,"y":2106,"width":1400,"height":70},
		{"id":"a300000000000002","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    O[\"observation\"] --> Bk[\"WAM backbone (swappable)\"]\n    P[\"proprio + commanded q̈_arm + est. F_ext\"] --> CC[\"coupling-conditioned latent (added)\"]\n    Bk --> Z[\"latent z_t\"]\n    CC --> Z\n    Z --> W[\"SHARED WRENCH HEAD (added)<br/>δ_base (A) + J_ext^T F_ext (C), per contact mode\"]\n    Z --> AH[\"autoregressive action head (added)<br/>base→torso→arm (B)\"]\n    W --> AH\n    style CC fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style W fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style AH fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#27ae60\n    style Bk fill:#eeeeee,stroke:#888888\n```","x":40,"y":2188,"width":1700,"height":420},
		{"id":"a300000000000003","type":"text","text":"*Backbone-agnostic: the three **green** modules are the contribution — a plug-in on **any** WAM backbone. The backbone grid (DINO-WM / UWM / V-JEPA / Cosmos / a PPO floor) proves the lift is the **coupling term, not the backbone**.*","x":40,"y":2628,"width":1700,"height":90},
		{"id":"a300000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Compose → CoWAM** (Coupling-aware World-Action Model)\n\nThe three **green** coupling clusters (WB.A, WB.B, WB.C) are the co-equal core. The three **cyan** mechanism clusters (WAM.A predict · Sim2Real.B ground · Embodied-AI.B verify) are the predict / ground / verify seams **and** standalone advances.\n\nImproving a cluster means advancing **all its directions together as one artifact** — not isolated point fixes. Core + mechanisms compose into **one deployable model: CoWAM**.","x":1780,"y":2188,"width":1380,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000006","type":"text","text":"**Part 1 · Coupling core (green)** — the co-equal spine","x":40,"y":2738,"width":1480,"height":30},
		{"id":"a300000000000007","type":"text","text":"**Part 2 · Mechanism clusters (cyan)** — predict / ground / verify, also standalone advances","x":1640,"y":2738,"width":1520,"height":30},
		{"id":"a300000000000010","type":"text","text":"**WB.A1 · CoReWA**\n[[2604.07993|HEX]] + [[2509.21231|SEEC]] + [[2506.14278|Heavy-Limbs WBC]]\n*Forecast arm latents into an anticipatory base reaction wrench feeding gate + controller.*","x":50,"y":2826,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000011","type":"text","text":"**WB.A2 · BlendBridge**\n[[2506.09366|SkillBlender]] + [[2602.08594|MOSAIC]] + [[2602.06341|HiWET]]\n*Entropy-gated per-joint residual adapts a frozen skill blend across the sim-to-real gap.*","x":50,"y":2994,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000012","type":"text","text":"**WB.A3 · ReachSched-WBT**\n[[2602.06341|HiWET]] + [[2508.11275|Diff. Reachability Maps]]\n*Schedule the base along a reachability gradient; shrink the margin with tracking residuals.*","x":50,"y":3162,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000013","type":"text","text":"**WB.A4 · CoLA-WB**\n[[2512.11047|WholeBodyVLA]] + [[2506.13751|LeVERB]] + [[2606.18772|HALOMI]]\n*Loco latent as residual of the manip code, projected onto a feasible manifold.*","x":50,"y":3330,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000014","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] Bet (WB.A)\n> Anticipating the arm-induced base wrench one horizon ahead cuts base-pose deviation + EE acceleration under fast reach-while-walking vs the implicit baseline — at no latency cost; zeroing the feed-forward path collapses the gain.","x":50,"y":3498,"width":460,"height":156},
		{"id":"a300000000000020","type":"text","text":"**WB.B1 · KCFlow-Strat**\n[[2503.05652|BRS]] + [[2507.01961|AC-DiT]] + [[2602.23024|InCoM]]\n*Stratified test of when one arm→base feasibility edge beats unidirectional base-first.*","x":570,"y":2826,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000021","type":"text","text":"**WB.B2 · LookAhead-WBC**\n[[2603.03243|HoMMI]] + [[2405.07991|SPIN]] + [[2411.04999|DynaMem]]\n*Memory-conditioned 3D look-at co-optimized with the base in one diffusion chunk.*","x":570,"y":2994,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000022","type":"text","text":"**WB.B3 · EchoPurge**\n[[2511.18112|EchoVLA]] + [[2411.04999|DynaMem]] + [[2510.07134|TrackVLA++]]\n*Differentiable in-policy purge gate + cross-visit re-ID for self-correcting multi-room memory.*","x":570,"y":3162,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000023","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] Bet (WB.B)\n> A single one-way arm→base feasibility edge captures nearly all the gain — concentrated on the reach-extension stratum, near-zero on fixed-base — while symmetric coupling buys latency, not accuracy.","x":570,"y":3330,"width":460,"height":156},
		{"id":"a300000000000030","type":"text","text":"**WB.C1 · PROWL**\n[[2505.06776|FALCON]] + [[2201.03871|ALMA]] + [[2606.16542|ADAPT]]\n*Momentum-observer residual forecasts hand wrench into FALCON's dual agents; legs pre-brace before loads peak. (ALMA's anticipatory mechanism is the transferable claim — its numbers are quadruped.)*","x":1090,"y":2826,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000031","type":"text","text":"**WB.C2 · PALADIN**\n[[2605.25546|ISSf-CBF WBC]] + [[2604.07457|CMP]] + [[2602.01515|RAPT]] (cross-check)\n*PROWL's forecast conformally bounded → re-sizes the ISSf-CBF QP + narrows CMP's radius; RAPT's residual demoted to a runtime cross-check.*","x":1090,"y":2994,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a300000000000032","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] Bet (WB.C)\n> A learned forecast channel cuts peak base-tilt + EE-tracking error in the first 0–300 ms after load onset for ramped loads (beating persistence) — and the same residual sizes a conformal safety bound.","x":1090,"y":3162,"width":460,"height":156},
		{"id":"a300000000000040","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A1 · GROVER**\n[[2605.20752|GaussianDream]] + [[2602.10098|VLA-JEPA]] + [[2605.06222|FFDC-WAM]]\n*Shared motion code grounds a leakage-free latent via a discardable 3D-Gaussian teacher; deploy gates on a calibrated residual.*","x":1650,"y":2826,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000041","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A2 · WrenchCast**\n[[2606.09337|TORL-VLA]] + [[2606.13877|ContactWorld]] + [[2603.17851|DexViTac]]\n*Rolls latent forward H steps; decodes a sensorless 6-DoF wrench split into self-motion + contact, with a conformal trust gate.*","x":1650,"y":2994,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000042","type":"text","text":"**WAM.A3 · DUET-WM**\n[[2605.06388|Semantic-LDM-WM]] + [[2503.00653|DC-MPC]] + [[2505.04999|CLAM]]\n*Splits a d=96 semantic latent into a continuous flow channel + an FSQ residual channel, per-token gated, CLAM-grounded.*","x":1650,"y":3162,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000043","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] Bet (WAM.A)\n> A latent grounded through a shared code or a training-only teacher yields a calibrated residual whose ECE + failure-detection AUROC beat the uncalibrated baseline and match the sensor-equipped ceiling — at sub-2× pure-latent deploy cost.","x":1650,"y":3330,"width":460,"height":156},
		{"id":"a300000000000050","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B1 · SENSE-T**\n[[2503.17973|PhysTwin]] + [[2511.04665|Real-to-Sim GS]] + [[2603.01151|D-REX]]\n*One differentiable rollout yields per-channel analytic sensitivity of sim-real divergence, replacing the discrete fidelity sweep.*","x":2170,"y":2826,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000051","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B2 · AMORTI-SIM**\n[[2603.01151|D-REX]] + [[2603.23973|SLAT-Phys]] + [[2410.20357|Dynamics-as-Prompts]]\n*Clutter-conditioned net predicts a novel object's full constitutive vector in one pass — zero per-object loops.*","x":2170,"y":2994,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000052","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B3 · FideliGate**\n[[2403.03949|RialTo]] + [[2504.03597|Real-is-Sim]] + [[2604.13645|CFG-ADDA]]\n*Photometric correction residual becomes a fidelity gate on fold-back demos, making rounds monotonically improve real success.*","x":2170,"y":3162,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000053","type":"text","text":"**S2R.B4 · CLaRe**\n[[2304.14369|NCLaw]] + [[2508.01112|MASIV]] + [[2603.22039|RAFL]]\n*Two-head MPM splits a constitutive law from a starved residual — making the split a falsifiable extrapolation measurement.*","x":2170,"y":3330,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000054","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] Bet (S2R.B)\n> Per-channel analytic sensitivity, fidelity-gated fold-back, and an identifiability-certified residual each beat the uniform-trust baseline by a monotone margin — and the same instrument certifies the robot's own coupling block only where it drove divergence below threshold.","x":2170,"y":3498,"width":460,"height":156},
		{"id":"a300000000000060","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B1 · CIC**\n[[2606.05773|PiL-World]] + [[2606.18610|SC3-Eval]] + [[2605.29360|MiraBench]]\n*Self-certifying action-counterfactual metric, U_cf-gated (ρ = 0.94 / 0.984 references).*","x":2690,"y":2826,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000061","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B2 · CALM**\n[[2606.03385|GTP-FA]] + [[2506.21669|SEEA-R1]] + [[2508.19236|MemoryVLA]]\n*Cause-attributed failure memory, channel-routed supervised correction, subspace-protected.*","x":2690,"y":2994,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000062","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B3 · ElastiVote**\n[[2507.05116|VOTE]] + [[2605.08799|ElasticFlow]] + [[2605.29438|ElegantVLA]]\n*One-NFE policy; span + backbone knobs; c_{t-1}-gated recompute at ≥ 30 Hz.*","x":2690,"y":3162,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000063","type":"text","text":"**EAI.B4 · GSE-Null**\n[[2602.21919|Null-Space Learning]] + [[2603.02224|Subspace-Geometry Forgetting]] + [[2605.06175|VLA-GSE]]\n*Two-space continual FT; null-space-protected wrench head; no forgetting.*","x":2690,"y":3330,"width":460,"height":156,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a300000000000064","type":"text","text":"> [!tip] Bet (EAI.B)\n> A validity-gated action-counterfactual metric predicts real-fleet success better than fidelity scores — and the same residual holds R² ≥ 0.70 with backward transfer ≥ -2 pp through deployment + re-training.","x":2690,"y":3498,"width":460,"height":156},
		{"id":"a400000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: before building anything expensive, three cheap falsifiers — one per coupling cluster — each testing the shared claim every direction in that cluster is built on, so a pass advances the whole cluster (its directions together), not one recipe. Same data, same backbone, same tasks, in sim, no new data. Per-cluster go/no-go: a cluster can fail without killing the others.*","x":20,"y":3770,"width":3160,"height":68},
		{"id":"a400000000000001","type":"text","text":"**WB.A cluster falsifier · arm↔leg** — three-way ablation, **stratified by arm-accel quartile**\n🟩 explicit-feedforward (ours) · 🟥 implicit ([[2604.07993|HEX]]-style, matched-capacity) · 🟥 reactive observer ([[2606.16542|ADAPT]])\n**Input-isolation:** identical head, swap _only_ the input — planned q̈_arm (anticipatory) vs the observer's measured estimate (reactive) — so any win is **feed-forward timing, not capacity**.\nA pass validates the anticipatory interface **A1–A4** all build on → the whole WB.A cluster advances together.","x":40,"y":3838,"width":1020,"height":200},
		{"id":"a400000000000002","type":"text","text":"**WB.C cluster falsifier · force-under-load (shares WB.A's head)** — same three-way under a **step-applied unknown load**, stratified by magnitude + direction\n🟩 anticipatory wrench-reaction (ours) · 🟥 reactive ([[2606.16542|ADAPT]] observer / [[2505.06776|FALCON]] curriculum / impedance) · 🟥 implicit\n**Headline-C:** first-100 ms **CoM-excursion advantage** after load onset, where reactive lags.\nA pass validates the forecast **C1** produces and **C2** certifies → both WB.C directions advance together.","x":1090,"y":3838,"width":1020,"height":200},
		{"id":"a400000000000003","type":"text","text":"**WB.B cluster falsifier · base↔arm (kinematic)**\n🟩 autoregressive base→torso→arm ([[2503.05652|BRS]]-style) · [[2507.01961|AC-DiT]] one-directional conditioning (middle rung) · 🟥 flat-concatenation ([[2401.02117|Mobile ALOHA]] floor)\n*Margin must **concentrate on reach-extension** (target outside the standing arm-workspace) and **vanish on fixed-base** reaches.*\nA pass validates the base-first backbone **B1** contributes, that **B2/B3** compound on → the whole WB.B loop advances together.","x":2140,"y":3838,"width":1020,"height":200},
		{"id":"a400000000000004","type":"text","text":"**The ε-curve — the de-circularization move (the cleverest single idea)**\nSupervise each force head on a **deliberately wrong** physics model (perturbed by ε) and report the win **as a function of model error ε**. If the explicit head still wins when its own supervision is wrong, the win is the **inductive bias, not label leakage**. That one curve is **both the headline figure and the falsification test**.","x":40,"y":4058,"width":1480,"height":200},
		{"id":"a400000000000005","type":"text","text":"> [!example] GO / NO-GO per cluster (illustrative — replace with measured)\n> **A:** margin ≥ 5 pp concentrated at high arm-accel **AND** anticipatory beats reactive by ≥ 5 pp\n> **C:** pre-registered first-100 ms CoM-excursion reduction ≥ 20% at matched load\n> **B:** ≥ 5 pp on reach-extension, near-zero on fixed-base\n> If explicit ≈ implicit on a cluster → **that bet is void** and the others continue.","x":1540,"y":4058,"width":1100,"height":200},
		{"id":"a400000000000006","type":"text","text":"🖼️ **Figure placeholder — expected result**\n*Drop the illustrative ε-curve / quartile chart here (swap for measured numbers once the falsifiers run): explicit wins, concentrated on the top arm-accel quartile, and the gap widens as the inertia model degrades.*","x":2660,"y":4058,"width":500,"height":200},
		{"id":"a500000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: the order is set by dependencies + gates, not a calendar. The cheap cluster falsifiers + de-risk checks come first because everything expensive depends on them; each build commits only after its gate clears. No paper-by-paper plan — just what to build per cluster and the go/no-go that green-lights the next.*","x":20,"y":4350,"width":3160,"height":56},
		{"id":"a500000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Phase 0 · de-risk** (before any training, in sim) — kill or confirm two existential risks per force cluster:\n\n• **Anticipatory window viable** — A: PR-0a reaction rise-time ≥ **31 ms** at top-quartile accel; C: first-100 ms window beats the composed onboard loop latency by ≥ 5 ms\n• **Physics identifiable** — PR-0b recover a planted inertia / contact model to ≤ **15% Frobenius**\n\nGates **pre-commit the scope**: anticipation fails → keep the grounded explicit-vs-implicit term; grounding fails → analytic term + broad DR; both fail → ship the de-circularized ε-curve only.","x":40,"y":4418,"width":1480,"height":300},
		{"id":"a500000000000002","type":"text","text":"**The builds & their gates (pre-registered)**\n\n| Build | Deliverable | Gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| **The three cluster falsifiers** (WB.A·WB.B·WB.C, parallel) | per-cluster three-way / autoregressive ablations + ε-curves | A ≥ 5 pp at high arm-accel **&** anticipatory > reactive ≥ 5 pp; C first-100 ms CoM-excursion ≥ 20%; B ≥ 5 pp reach-extension, ~0 fixed-base |\n| **Ground the terms** | diff. sysID of M(base,arm) (A) + contact model / J_ext (C) on the real robot; B's object physics rides the engine's native recovery | ≤ 15% Frobenius **&** beats broad-DR on OOD mass/load **&** ≥ 80% real-SR retention |\n| **CoWAM** | shared wrench head, sensor-free forecast of self-induced (A) + external (C) reaction | sensor-free wrench MSE ≤ 2× tactile-available baseline on [[2604.13015\\|Touch Dreaming]] (w/o-Touch) + [[2403.10506\\|HumanoidBench]] taxel-toggle |\n| **Verify + continual** | causal-consistency metric across all three clusters + hardware | predicted-vs-realized R² ≥ 0.70 **&** continual lift retained (NBT ≥ -2 pp) |","x":1540,"y":4418,"width":1620,"height":300},
		{"id":"a500000000000003","type":"text","text":"**Cheap go/no-go first.** The three cluster falsifiers + the verify track run first; the costly downstream builds (ground · CoWAM · verify-on-hardware) **commit only after the falsifiers' gate clears**.\nThe de-risked core needs **no WAM** — the force heads are MLPs on proprio + commanded q̈_arm / est. F_ext — so it banks the go/no-go + the causal-consistency metric cheaply on the lean `humanoid-bench` PPO substrate.","x":40,"y":4738,"width":720,"height":210,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a500000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Per-cluster gating, co-equal.** Each cluster's gate unblocks its own downstream build — **WB.B → action head**; **WB.A + WB.C → shared wrench head**; none is the master gate. CoWAM then deploys real-time on the real humanoid, verified by the causal-consistency metric, with the **backbone-agnostic coupling grid** as the centerpiece (lift = coupling term, not backbone).","x":800,"y":4738,"width":720,"height":210,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a500000000000005","type":"text","text":"**No paper-by-paper plan** — just what to build per cluster and the go/no-go that green-lights the next. All three coupling clusters advance together; a cluster can fail independently and **every branch still yields a result**.","x":1560,"y":4738,"width":720,"height":210,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a500000000000006","type":"text","text":"**C2 · certified safe set** — *deferred extension of WB.C* 🟪\nA barrier / QP guaranteeing balance + collision-freeness under load. Opened **only once** the coupling is predicted, grounded, and verified.","x":2320,"y":4738,"width":840,"height":210,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a500000000000007","type":"text","text":"**Feasibility — robot · compute · code.** Real Unitree **H1** (Shadow Hands + 448-taxel tactile) for the grounded story, **G1** for lighter deploy. Falsifiers: days on a few GPUs; CoWAM: days-to-weeks on a multi-GPU node; deploy on a Jetson Orin at ≥ 30 Hz. **327 repos already cloned** with named fork targets (`humanoid-bench`/`HEX`, `FALCON`/`ADAPT`, `brs-algo`/`AC-DiT`, `D-rex`/`gradsim`, `dino_wm`/`UWM`/`vjepa2`, `stable-worldmodel`/`VLA-GSE`).","x":40,"y":4968,"width":3120,"height":120},
		{"id":"a600000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: humanoid benchmarks only — the same suites the anchor papers run on. The mechanism clusters are measured on these too; a non-humanoid tabletop suite would not test a humanoid-optimized WAM. (MobileManiBench, ContactWorld, MS-HAB, ManiFeel are non-humanoid — out.)*","x":20,"y":5180,"width":3160,"height":56},
		{"id":"a600000000000001","type":"text","text":"**WB.A arm↔leg — balance / disturbance / whole-body loco-manip** 🟧 *headline axis*\n[[2403.10506|HumanoidBench]] (standard) · [[2603.20147|AGILE]] · [[2606.17833|HumanoidArena]] · [[2503.05652|BRS]] (Galaxea R1) · [[2506.09366|SkillBench]] · [[2506.13751|LeVERB-Bench]] · [[2308.14636|Disturbance-Rejection]] + [[2404.19173|Single-Contact++]] (Digit impact) · [[2602.13656|KungFuAthlete]] · [[2508.19926|FARM]] · [[2602.13850|Humanoid-Hanoi]] · [[2511.17925|Switch-JustDance]] · [[2602.21599|Iterative Closed-Loop]] · [[2507.18883|Partial-Obs Loco]] · [[2307.10142|Potential-Based Rewards]] · [[2408.00342|MuJoCo-MPC-HB]]","x":40,"y":5248,"width":1020,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a600000000000002","type":"text","text":"**WB.B base↔arm — humanoid mobile-manipulation** 🟧 *headline axis*\n[[2407.07788|BiGym]] (Unitree H1 bimanual mobile-manip) · [[2503.05652|BRS]] (Galaxea R1 whole-body).\n\n*The common mobile-manip suites (MobileManiBench, MS-HAB) are non-humanoid → not used.*","x":1090,"y":5248,"width":1020,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a600000000000003","type":"text","text":"**WB.C force-under-load — external wrench / contact** 🟧 *headline axis*\n[[2505.06776|FALCON]] force-curriculum · [[2510.26280|Thor]] (167.7 N pull) · [[2606.03297|SplitAdapter]] (6 kg OOD) · contact wrench on [[2604.13015|Touch Dreaming]] (real, L_force head + w/o-Touch ablation) + [[2403.10506|HumanoidBench]] taxel-toggle arm · [[2510.25725|Humanoid Visual-Tactile-Action]] (tactile dataset).","x":2140,"y":5248,"width":1020,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a600000000000004","type":"text","text":"**Real-robot sim2real (humanoid)** — [[2602.01515|RAPT]] humanoid sim2real OOD, on the H1 / G1 deploy from Row 5.","x":40,"y":5508,"width":1480,"height":120},
		{"id":"a600000000000005","type":"text","text":"**The backbone grid** — { PPO floor, [[2411.04983|DINO-WM]], [[2504.02792|UWM]], [[2501.03575|Cosmos]], [[2603.14482|V-JEPA 2.1]] } × { coupling off / on }, on the humanoid benchmarks above. Within-backbone paired off/on **isolates the lift** → shows the lift is the coupling term, not the backbone.","x":1540,"y":5508,"width":1620,"height":120},
		{"id":"a700000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: a de-risked program, not a single fragile bet. Each channel can fail independently, and every failure mode still produces a result.*","x":20,"y":5720,"width":3160,"height":56},
		{"id":"a700000000000001","type":"text","text":"**Risks & fallbacks — every branch yields a result**\n\n| Risk | Fallback (still a result) |\n|---|---|\n| **Explicit ≈ implicit** on a cluster | I still own that cluster's definitive three-way explicit / implicit / reactive ablation with the ε-sweep |\n| **Wrong / unidentifiable inertia or contact model** | analytic term + broad domain randomization for that cluster (grounding seam dropped); the ablation still ships |\n| **Base↔arm factoring buys little, or its decode adds latency (B)** | report the autoregressive-vs-flat margin stratified by reach-extension (PR-1B), not pooled; parallelize / distill the decode if latency bites; the definitive ablation still ships |\n| **C first-100 ms hostage to composed loop latency** | price the whole onboard budget (PR-0a-C); if it eats the window, move the C headline to a steady-state max-load number |\n| **Hardware-dominant physics** (foot-contact / friction / actuator swamp the term) | instrument the residual budget first (PR-0a'); scope down if the term is dominated |\n| **WAM too slow for contact** | async decoupling + quantization clear the ≥ 30 Hz floor; report the SR-vs-Hz Pareto honestly |","x":40,"y":5788,"width":2000,"height":330},
		{"id":"a700000000000002","type":"text","text":"> [!warning] The one risk the direction absorbs\n> The explicit heads need a half-decent physics model — a wrong URDF or contact model poisons them, and then explicit ≈ implicit. This is exactly why **grounding (differentiable system-ID) is in the core, not the extension**. If sysID can't be learned cleanly on a channel, the fallback is that channel's implicit / reactive baseline — and I've still produced the definitive ablation, which the verify metric makes publishable either way.","x":2080,"y":5788,"width":1080,"height":300},
		{"id":"a800000000000000","type":"text","text":"*Speaker note: I want your sign-off on the direction before I commit the next phase, and a steer on sequencing.*","x":20,"y":6180,"width":3160,"height":56},
		{"id":"a800000000000001","type":"text","text":"**What I am asking — your endorsement of the full program direction.**\nThe shape: the **green** coupling core (WB.A arm↔leg, WB.B base↔arm, WB.C force-under-load) as the co-equal spine, with the **cyan** mechanism clusters (WAM.A predict, Sim2Real.B ground, Embodied-AI.B verify) complementary — each a standalone embodied-AI advance that also wires the predict / ground / verify loop onto the coupling.\n\n1. Is the **explicit, anticipatory coupling bet** (predict the cross-term, ground it, verify predicted = realized) the right thing to pursue across these six clusters?\n2. The first experiments are cheap, parallel, self-falsifying (~6 months, no new data) — **which clusters should I prioritize first?**\n\n*What I most want from this meeting: an early read on the framing + the cluster set.*","x":40,"y":6248,"width":2000,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a800000000000002","type":"text","text":"**Cross-references**\n• [[Focus-Direction]] — the explicit-coupling thesis this pitch reduces from\n• [[Focus-Direction-Research-Plan]] + [[Focus-Direction-Research-Plan-detailed]] — lean & full-rigor plans\n• [[Focus-Direction-Paper-Code-Index]] — every cited paper → KH note + cloned repo\n• Source clusters: [[Whole-Body]] (A / B / C), [[WAM]] (predict), [[Sim2Real]] (ground), [[Embodied-AI]] (verify)","x":2080,"y":6248,"width":1080,"height":260},
		{"id":"a2f0000000000001","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2604.07993-method.png","x":40,"y":1379,"width":370,"height":110},
		{"id":"a2f0000000000002","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2606.16542-method.png","x":430,"y":1379,"width":370,"height":167},
		{"id":"a2f0000000000003","type":"file","file":"data/figures/2507.01961-method.png","x":840,"y":1379,"width":274,"height":200},
		{"id":"a2f0000000000004","type":"text","x":1166,"y":1379,"width":370,"height":200,"text":"🖼️ **Mobile ALOHA** — flat base+arm concatenation\n*(the naive floor; no architecture figure available)*"}
	],
